<title>USA: Continental Materials hires adviser.</title>
<headline>Continental Materials hires adviser.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Materials Corp said Monday the special committee of its board of directors hired Chicago Corp as its financial advisor to assist in responding to a proposal to take the company private.</p>
<p>The proposal was made by a shareholder group consisting of chief executive officer James Gidwitz and other members of his family.</p>
<p>On November 22, the heating and cooling equipment maker said it had been named in three lawsuits filed by shareholders aimed at blocking the company from completing the transaction to go private.</p>
<p>Continental shares closed unchanged at 21-1/4 Monday.</p>
<p>	 ((--Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787)).</p>
